```javascript
function move(state, amount, fail = false) {
  if (fail || !Number.isInteger(amount) || amount < 0 || amount > state.available) {
    return { ...state };
  }
  return {
    available: state.available - amount,
    saved: state.saved + amount
  };
}
const original = { available: 24, saved: 2 };
console.log(move(original, 6));
console.log(move(original, 30));
console.log(move(original, 6, true));
console.log(original);
```
The valid move returns available: 18 and saved: 8, keeping the total 26. Invalid input or a forced failure keeps 24 and 2. The original stays unchanged. This models an invariant: a fact that must remain true after an allowed change.

